\fBMETHODS\fR
All known possible HTTP methods.
.TP
\fBSTATUS_CODES\fR
A mapping of status codes to status texts
.TP
\fBAgentOptions (extends undefined)\fR
An options object container for an `Agent` instance.
.TP
\fBAgent (extends undefined)\fR
An Agent is responsible for managing connection persistence and reuse for HTTPS clients.
.TP
\fBClientRequest (extends undefined)\fR
An object that is created internally and returned from `request()`.
.TP
\fBOutgoingMessage (extends undefined)\fR
The parent class of `ClientRequest` and `ServerResponse`. It is an abstract outgoing message from the perspective of the participants of an HTTP transaction.
.TP
\fBIncomingMessage (extends undefined)\fR
An `IncomingMessage` object is created by `Server` or `ClientRequest` and passed as the first argument to the 'request' and 'response' event respectively. It may be used to access response status, headers, and data.
.TP
\fBServerResponse (extends undefined)\fR
An object that is created internally by a `Server` instance, not by the user. It is passed as the second parameter to the 'request' event.
.TP
\fBConnection (extends undefined)\fR
A duplex stream between a HTTP request `IncomingMessage` and the response `ServerResponse`
.TP
\fBServer (extends undefined)\fR
A nodejs compat HTTP server typically intended for running in a "worker" environment.
.TP
\fBglobalAgent\fR
The global and default HTTPS agent.
.TP
\fBrequest(optionsOrURL, options, callback)\fR
Makes a HTTPS request, optionally a `oro://` for relative paths when `oro:` is the origin protocol.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptionsOrURL\fR (string \\| object; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object \\| function; optional)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIClientRequest\fR
.TP
\fBget(optionsOrURL, options, callback)\fR
Makes a HTTPS or `oro:` GET request. A simplified alias to `request()`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptionsOrURL\fR (string \\| object; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object \\| function; optional)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIClientRequest\fR
.TP
\fBcreateServer(...args)\fR
Creates a HTTPS server that can listen for incoming requests. Requests that are dispatched to this server depend on the context in which it is created, such as a service worker which will use a "fetch event" adapter.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object \\| function; optional)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIServer\fR
